# ---------------------------------------------------------------- stage 5 ----
# NPT compression to the operating state, at elevated pressure.
#
# This has to be done under load. Collapsing a 0.35 g/cm3 packing to melt
# density at 1 atm is barostat-limited: the driving force is the ambient
# pressure itself, and the cell creeps. Measured on the validation system, 30k
# steps of iso 1.0 reached 0.70 g/cm3 and stopped climbing -- 35% below a real
# dry AEM, which would have been reported as a converged dry membrane and
# inflated every uptake number downstream, since the water goes into the voids
# that should not be there.
#
# The fix is the standard melt-densification cycle: compress hot and hard, then
# release to the operating pressure and let the density relax back up to its
# equilibrium value from the dense side rather than creeping toward it from the
# dilute side.
fix             npt_squeeze all npt temp 600.0 600.0 100.0 iso 1000.0 1000.0 1000.0
run             20000
